  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At a poetry competition he praises the students’ scholarly aura and credits Brother Jiang’s teachings. After calling their literary battle a tie, he proposes a passing-the-flower game so three winning students can recite poems, then opens his eyes and asks who holds the red flower.",
      "chapters": [
        1824
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_teacher_jiang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He smiles and nods when Li Xiao Bai greets the teachers, laughs when the student takes another turn under the rules, and praises a poem’s final line. Using a method to inspect literary qi and talent qi, he finds ordinary talent and takes no suspicion, calling Li Xiao Bai very honest.",
      "chapters": [
        1825
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "judging-li-xiao-bai",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_li_xiao_bai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Li Xiao Bai later recalls that Great Scholar Shen, who competed against Teacher Jiang, was one of the ten great scholars in a past selection, yet remains at rank five peak stage for lack of outstanding political talent or a powerful background. Teacher Jiang and Great Scholar Shen are said to have wandered outside the Imperial Court rather than become officials, one opening a private school while the other roamed everywhere, with immortal ascension nearly hopeless under Imperial Court control of immortal materials.",
      "chapters": [
        1870
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ten-great-scholars",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_imperial_court"
      ]
    }
